# Vina-Ion-Metal v1.0.2 validation log - GlfT2 crystal redocking (Mn2+ site)
#
# System: galactofuranosyltransferase GlfT2, PDB 4FIY chain A, Mn2+ (residue 702).
# Ligand: examples/glft2/ligand.pdbqt = deposited 4FIY UDP (chain A, residue 701),
#   prepared with Meeko; the crystal coordinates are preserved exactly
#   (max deviation 0.000 A). In the deposited pose the UDP coordinates Mn2+
#   through O1B (2.79 A) and O1A (2.89 A); those oxygens are typed as the
#   unprotonated (=O) sites in the PDBQT.
# Command (run inside examples/glft2): vina --config config.txt --out glft2_out.pdbqt
#   seed 42, exhaustiveness 16, num_modes 9, box 22 A at (142.54, 32.19, 48.55),
#   --metals auto (implicit in config.txt).
# Binary: Vina-Ion-Metal v1.0.2, Linux x86-64, static Boost 1.83 build.
#   Reported affinities are metal-aware since v1.0.2 (fix F6: the coordination
#   term is no longer cancelled out of the reported energy). Global-search
#   trajectories depend on the Boost version; fixed-pose scores do not.
# Post-run analysis (NOT printed by Vina; symmetry-aware heavy-atom RMSD vs the
#   deposited UDP pose via RDKit GetBestRMS, O-Mn distances from the PDBQT):
#   mode 1 (top-ranked, -8.861): RMSD 1.50 A, coordinates Mn2+ with three
#     oxygens at 2.12/2.18/2.51 A;
#   modes 2-9: RMSD 1.75/2.37/1.40/1.96/1.83/1.66/1.54/0.64 A,
#     affinities -8.806/-8.781/-8.654/-8.622/-8.420/-8.413/-8.334/-8.310;
#   all nine modes coordinate Mn2+ (minimum O-Mn 2.10-2.62 A, within the
#   Harding Mn-O range ~2.15 A; the crystal coordination itself is 2.79/2.89 A).
#   Rescoring mode 1 with --score_only reproduces the printed affinity to
#   0.002 kcal/mol (pre-F6 binaries were internally inconsistent by ~1.4).
#
# Raw command output follows.
